Why AGPL-3.0
------------
The Python training, export, benchmarking and tracking scripts are built on
Ultralytics YOLO (ultralytics==8.4.184), which is licensed under AGPL-3.0.
Ultralytics states that models trained with its software fall under AGPL-3.0
by default. Using the same licence for the whole repository keeps the code and
any weights or TensorRT engines released from it under one consistent set of
terms.

Third-party software (installed as dependencies; not included here)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
- Ultralytics YOLO - AGPL-3.0 - https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
- TrackEval - fetched by scripts/run_stage4.sh; see its repository for terms -
  https://github.com/JonathonLuiten/TrackEval
- NVIDIA TensorRT and CUDA, ONNX, ONNX Runtime and OpenCV - each under its own
  licence

Data
----
VisDrone2019 (Zhu et al., "Detection and Tracking Meet Drones Challenge",
IEEE TPAMI 2021; https://github.com/VisDrone/VisDrone-Dataset) is not
redistributed in this repository; it is downloaded from its providers. The
official repository does not state a licence; redistributions of the dataset
describe it as licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 (non-commercial). Models trained
on it, including any weights or TensorRT engines released by this project,
are provided for non-commercial research use.
